    "ImageDescription": {
      "value": "<p>Ball-and-stick model of the <b><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tyrosine\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"w:Tyrosine\">tyrosine</a></b> molecule, one of the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Proteinogenic_amino_acid\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"w:Proteinogenic amino acid\">20 amino acids</a> used to build proteins. This image shows the L isomer in neutral form.\n</p><p><b>Colour code:</b>\n</p>\n<dl><dd><b style=\"display:inline-block;line-height:1.7;width:1.7em;margin-right:-1px;border:1px solid #808080;background:#505050\" title=\"#505050\"> </b> Carbon, C: black<br></dd>\n<dd><b style=\"display:inline-block;line-height:1.7;width:1.7em;margin-right:-1px;border:1px solid #808080;background:#F0F0F0\" title=\"#F0F0F0\"> </b> Hydrogen, H: white<br></dd>\n<dd><b style=\"display:inline-block;line-height:1.7;width:1.7em;margin-right:-1px;border:1px solid #808080;background:#F51E1E\" title=\"#F51E1E\"> </b> Oxygen, O: red<br></dd>\n<dd><b style=\"display:inline-block;line-height:1.7;width:1.7em;margin-right:-1px;border:1px solid #808080;background:#3C50FA\" title=\"#3C50FA\"> </b> Nitrogen, N: blue<br></dd></dl>",
      "source": "commons-desc-page"
    },
